    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.pairs\n\n### Description\n\nI don't have a lot of hope for this but would it be possible to add support for method/function call bracket autocompete triggered by `nvim-cmp`? In essence what this function https://github.com/windwp/nvim-autopairs/blob/master/lua/nvim-autopairs/completion/cmp.lua#L51 does. Look at the LSP kind and if it's a function/method add brackets?\r\n\r\nIt could be a generic piece of code that mini.completion could use to achieve the same effect if the `confirm_done` equivalent callback in mini.completion provided the same data?",
